   "text": "Confirmed: [4, 13, 15] with signs [1, -1, -1] achieves an in-sample Sharpe of 0.592, robustly the best found across ~70 evaluations covering all singles, many pairs, and triplet neighborhoods.\n\nNow let me reason about out-of-sample expectations. In-sample Sharpe of 0.592 on 3 combined (fairly uncorrelated, weak) signals, built via search over 40 features with ~70 evaluations, likely has meaningful overfitting/selection bias. Individual feature Sharpes were modest (0.13\u20130.39 in magnitude), and combining 3 roughly orthogonal weak signals can genuinely produce a Sharpe of ~0.3-0.6 in expectation if the underlying signal is real, but I should shade down for selection bias from testing many combinations.\n\nI'll submit this specification with a conservative predicted OOS Sharpe."
